{"id":580537003,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODA1MzcwMDM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdextension","name":"topic:gdextension","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1609442062,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjA5NDQyMDYy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:shaders","name":"topic:shaders","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-24T09:46:00Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T09:54:56Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.5\ngodot-cpp 4.5\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn Godot,  the `set_include_path` function isn't bound within `Shader::_bind_methods`. So in godot-cpp, that function of the `Shader` class isn't defined.\n\nWhen compiling a shader without include path, the asset path  is used as a fallback. But shaders created from code don’t have an asset path. So in a C++ extension, the only solution is to set the shader’s asset path to the include path before its compilation, then set it back to an empty string.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nNone\n\nCompare Godot's `Shader` class to the godot-cpp one: `set_include_path` is missing.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNone","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116712/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116712/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}